		'as-relacoes-de-casal-na-nova-era' => array(
			'en_slug'             => 'couple-relationships-in-the-new-era',
			'en_title'            => 'Couple Relationships in the New Era',
			'en_excerpt'          => 'What are couple relationships for today, now that surviving together is no longer the point?',
			'en_meta_description' => 'Why the purpose of relationships is shifting from surviving together to living with awareness — and what that asks of couples today.',
			'en_content'          => '<h3>When the purpose stops being about surviving together and becomes about living with awareness</h3>
</p>
<p><em><strong>Text: Juliana Gomes</strong></em></p>
<p><em><strong>Founder of Escola Mulher Sistêmica</strong></em></p>
<p><em><strong>Instagram: </strong></em><u><strong><a href="https://www.instagram.com/juliana.mendes.gomes/" rel="nofollow">https://www.instagram.com/juliana.mendes.gomes/</a></strong></u></p>
</p>
<p><u><a href="https://mulhersistemica.my.canva.site/adultecer-para-amar" rel="nofollow">https://mulhersistemica.my.canva.site/adultecer-para-amar</a></u></p>
</p>
<p>We are in the week of Valentine\'s Day.</p>
<p>A time when shop windows fill up with hearts, social media floods with declarations of love and, inevitably, we are invited to reflect on our relationships.</p>
<p>But perhaps the most important question is not whether we are loving or being loved.</p>
<p>Perhaps the question is:</p>
<h5>What are couple relationships for in the times we live in?</h5>
</p>
<p>This is a question that has run through my work with women over the last few years. And the more I observe their stories, their challenges and their processes of transformation, the more I see that we are living through a profound change in the way we understand love, partnership and life as a couple.</p>
<p>For thousands of years, relationships had a very clear function: to guarantee the continuity of life.</p>
<p>Our ancestors joined together in order to survive.</p>
<p>Marriages were, above all, structures that sustained the family, the household economy, protection and reproduction. Love could exist, but it was not necessarily the centre of the choice.</p>
<p>Survival was.</p>
</p>
<p>It was through this model that life reached us.</p>
<p>And it is important to acknowledge that with respect.</p>
<p>Life crossed wars, scarcity, illness, losses, inequalities and countless challenges in order to keep existing. Our parents, grandparents and great-grandparents carried burdens we often cannot even imagine.</p>
<p>That is why we also inherited deep beliefs about relationships.</p>
<p>The idea that loving requires sacrifice.</p>
<p>The idea that we must endure.</p>
<p>The idea that individual happiness must be put second in order to preserve the family.</p>
</p>
<p>The idea that staying is always better than leaving.</p>
<p>But something is changing.</p>
<p>For the first time in history, millions of people are asking themselves not only how to survive, but how to live.</p>
<p>The search for therapy, self-knowledge, spirituality, personal development and emotional health has never been so intense.</p>
<p>People want to understand who they are.</p>
<p>They want to discover their purposes.</p>
<p>They want to find meaning.</p>
</p>
<p>And when individuals change, relationships inevitably change too.</p>
<p>Perhaps that is why we see so many questions arising.</p>
<p>Couples who choose not to have children.</p>
<p>Women who decide to postpone motherhood.</p>
<p>New family configurations.</p>
<p>Separations that once seemed unthinkable.</p>
<p>People seeking different ways of building a shared life.</p>
<p>I do not believe we are witnessing the end of love.</p>
<p>I believe we are witnessing the end of a model of relationship that no longer answers the needs of a new consciousness.</p>
<p>The data reinforce this perception.</p>
<p>Brazil has been recording record numbers of divorces, and a significant share of those separations happens before even ten years of relationship.</p>
<p>But perhaps the question is not why relationships are ending.</p>
<p>Perhaps the question is: what did they come to teach us?</p>
<p>In my experience, couple relationships remain one of the greatest paths of self-knowledge available to a human being.</p>
</p>
<p>It is in the encounter with the other that our wounds appear.</p>
<p>It is in the everydayness of living together that our needs, fears, expectations and unconscious patterns reveal themselves.</p>
<p>The other becomes a mirror.</p>
<p>And we do not always like what we see reflected.</p>
<p>Perhaps that is why so many women begin their therapeutic processes motivated by relational pain.</p>
<p>Many arrive hoping to save a relationship.</p>
<p>But they end up finding themselves.</p>
<p>They discover that some questions are not about the partner.</p>
<p>They are about them.</p>
<p>About their limits.</p>
<p>About their self-esteem.</p>
<p>About their family history.</p>
<p>About the way they learned to love.</p>
<p>About what they believe they deserve.</p>
<p>And here one of the greatest challenges of contemporary relationships arises.</p>
<p>What happens when one person grows and the other stays in the same place?</p>
<p>What happens when a woman begins to expand her awareness, look at her pain, review her beliefs and build a new relationship with herself?</p>
<p>This is a delicate question, but a necessary one.</p>
<p>Because relationships are not made up of love alone.</p>
<p>They are made up of exchanges.</p>
</p>
<p>Of shared responsibility.</p>
<p>Of common purpose.</p>
<p>Of willingness to grow.</p>
<p>No relationship can evolve beyond the level of consciousness of the people who make it up.</p>
<p>Perhaps that is why New Era relationships demand something that was not so necessary before: deep conversations about purpose.</p>
<p>Not only about children.</p>
<p>Not only about money.</p>
<p>Not only about where to live or which goals to reach.</p>
<p>But about who we are becoming.</p>
<p>About which life we want to build.</p>
<p>About which values we wish to sustain.</p>
</p>
<p>About which consciousness we want to cultivate together.</p>
<p>I believe the new purpose of couple relationships is not only to guarantee that life continues.</p>
<p>I believe it is to help life flourish.</p>
<p>To create spaces where two people can grow, mature, awaken and expand their consciousness without having to abandon themselves in order to stay together.</p>
<p>Perhaps our ancestors joined together to guarantee the survival of life.</p>
<p>Perhaps our generation is being invited to learn something different.</p>
<p>To learn to live this life with more truth.</p>
<p>More presence.</p>
<p>More freedom.</p>
<p>And more awareness.</p>
</p>
<p>Because, in the end, perhaps New Era love is not about finding someone who completes us.</p>
</p>
<p>Perhaps it is about finding someone willing to walk beside us while both of us keep transforming.</p>
</p>
<p><u><a href="https://mulhersistemica.my.canva.site/adultecer-para-amar" rel="nofollow">https://mulhersistemica.my.canva.site/adultecer-para-amar</a></u></p>
',
