		'atividade-fisica-nao-deve-ser-um-projeto-de-verao-deve-ser-um-projeto-de-vida' => array(
			'en_slug'             => 'physical-activity-a-project-for-life',
			'en_title'            => 'Physical Activity Should Not Be a Summer Project, It Should Be a Project for Life.',
			'en_excerpt'          => 'Twelve-week challenges produce twelve-week results. A personal trainer on why the habits you can keep matter more than fast fixes.',
			'en_meta_description' => 'Why 12-week weight-loss programmes fail, and how strength training and habits you can sustain beat extreme diets and endless cardio.',
			'en_content'          => '<p><em><strong>Text: Ana Paula, Personal Trainer</strong></em></p>
<p><u><a href="https://www.instagram.com/fitandstrongwithana/" rel="nofollow">https://www.instagram.com/fitandstrongwithana/</a></u></p>
</p>
<p>It is very common to see “12 weeks to lose X kilos” programmes. And, along with them, come extreme solutions: exhausting workouts every day and severe food restriction. Yes, this can even produce fast weight loss… but the most important question is: could you keep that lifestyle going?</p>
</p>
<p>Probably not. Because it is not sustainable.</p>
</p>
<p>And here is a truth, based on my own experience: I lost 35 kg and have kept that result for more than 7 years. What many people do not realise is that the habits that made me lose weight are, to a great extent, the same ones that help me keep the weight off today. Of course, I make adjustments according to the phase of life,  but the foundation stays the same.</p>
</p>
<p>There is no shortcut. There is consistency.</p>
</p>
<p>Another important point: physical activity should not be seen only as a tool to “burn calories”. And, above all, cardio alone is not the best strategy for weight loss.</p>
</p>
<p>Strength training (weight training) is fundamental in this process. It helps preserve and increase muscle mass, which improves metabolism and contributes to more lasting results. Cardio, on the other hand, has an essential role for cardiovascular health, energy and well-being, and should not be seen only as a means of losing weight.</p>
</p>
<p>If you want to improve something in this process, start by changing your mindset:</p>
<p>instead of chasing fast results, chase habits that you can sustain.</p>
</p>
<p>Because in the end, what brings results is not what you do for 12 weeks, it is what you can keep for life!</p>
</p>
<p><em><strong>Movement is medicine!</strong></em></p>
<p><strong>To age with health, independence and quality of life, we need to stay strong.</strong></p>
',
