		'coragem-a-estrela-que-ilumina-o-caminho-do-empreendedor-especial-de-natal' => array(
			'en_slug'             => 'courage-the-star-that-lights-the-entrepreneurs-path',
			'en_title'            => 'Courage! The Star That Lights the Entrepreneur\'s Path — Christmas Special',
			'en_excerpt'          => 'Christmas lights remind us of the flame we so often let go out: courage. A short reflection for entrepreneurs closing the year.',
			'en_meta_description' => 'A Christmas reflection for entrepreneurs on why courage, not money or qualifications, keeps a business moving forward.',
			'en_content'          => '</p>
<p><strong>The end of the year always invites us to pause for </strong><u><strong>reflection.</strong></u></p>
<p>Christmas lights illuminate not only the streets of our cities, but also something we so often let go out along the entrepreneurial journey: the flame of courage.</p>
<p>Being an entrepreneur is, above all, an act of faith. Faith in an idea, faith in a purpose, faith in your own ability to get up after every stumble. Because stumbles will come, and they are not a sign of weakness.</p>
<p>​</p>
<p>They are part of the route. In fact, nobody builds anything extraordinary by walking in a straight line. Great business stories are born exactly in the detours, in the course corrections, in the ability to stop, take a deep breath and decide to try again.And here is a truth few will tell you. Money is not enough.</p>
</p>
<p>An academic background is not enough. It is not enough to have taken every course, been through mentoring, studied diligently. These elements help a great deal, but they do not sustain a business on their own. The backbone of entrepreneurship, yesterday, today and always, is courage! Courage to start.Courage to take calculated risks and uncalculated ones.Courage to recalculate the route a thousand times, if need be.</p>
</p>
<p>Courage to carry on, even when nobody else understands what you see.While some believe that entrepreneurship is about strategy, others think it is about capital. But we know: entrepreneurship is about heart. About putting your soul into every attempt and understanding that growth is not a destination, it is a continuous movement.</p>
</p>
<p>This Christmas, allow yourself to celebrate not only the results, but above all the journey. Celebrate the attempts, the falls, the fresh starts. Celebrate every time you dared to believe, even when everything seemed uncertain.</p>
</p>
<p>And may the coming year bring new routes, new ideas, new possibilities and the courage needed to follow them.Happy Christmas!</p>
</p>
<p>May this season renew your strength, your faith and your determination to keep creating, daring and building.</p>',
			'link_map'            => array(),
		),
		'cupcake-da-granny' => array(
			'en_slug'             => 'grannys-cupcake',
			'en_title'            => 'GRÁNNY\'S CUPCAKE',
			'en_excerpt'          => 'A budget-friendly cupcake batter that bakes up light and moist, plus a gourmet brigadeiro topping from Chef Sonia Campos.',
			'en_meta_description' => 'A budget-friendly cupcake recipe from Chef Sonia Campos, with a gourmet brigadeiro topping or filling for every cake.',
			'en_content'          => '<p><strong>Chef Sonia Campos</strong><strong> </strong><u><strong>@grannymadeireland</strong></u></p>
</p>
<p>Thinking about the cost of ingredients, I developed this perfect batter! Budget-friendly, it comes out light, moist and super simple to make.</p>
<p>It can be made in a blender, or even mixed by hand with a whisk.</p>
</p>
<p><em>The kids will love it!!!</em></p>
</p>
<h5>WRITE DOWN THE RECIPE: </h5>
</p>
<p>1 large egg (60g) 250g whole milk</p>
<p>1 cup 115g soya or sunflower oil </p>
<p>Half a cup 240g plain flour</p>
<p>2 cups 180g sugar </p>
<p>1 cup 30g cocoa powder 50% </p>
<p>2 tablespoons 15g baking powder</p>
<p>1 tablespoon of cornflour</p>
</p>
<p>Tip: TO MAKE THE WHITE BATTER, JUST LEAVE OUT THE COCOA</p>
<p>POWDER AND ADD 15ML OF VANILLA ESSENCE OR</p>
<p>SCRAPINGS FROM A VANILLA POD.</p>
</p>
<p>Blend everything in the blender for 5 min. </p>
<p>Pour into a bowl and gradually add the sifted plain flour, mix well and, last of all,</p>
<p>add the baking powder. Bake in a preheated oven at 180 degrees.</p>
</p>
<p>GOURMET BRIGADEIRO TOPPING: </p>
<p>1 tin of</p>
<p>condensed milk, </p>
<p>200g of cream, </p>
<p>20g of cocoa powder, </p>
<p>100g of chocolate blend, milk or dark </p>
<p>15g of unsalted butter (this gives the topping extra shine). </p>
<p>Bring to the heat, stirring slowly, until it reaches the thick ribbon stage. Leave it to cool and cover your</p>
<p>cupcakes.</p>
</p>
<p>Another option: instead of topping them, you can fill your cupcakes</p>
<p>with this brigadeiro.</p>
',
