		'dois-anos-novos-um-medido-pelo-homem-outro-sentido-pela-terra' => array(
			'en_slug'             => 'two-new-years-measured-by-man-felt-by-the-earth',
			'en_title'            => 'Two New Years: One Measured by Man, Another Felt by the Earth',
			'en_excerpt'          => 'The Gregorian calendar organises society, while the solar return — when the Sun enters Aries — governs vitality. Learning to honour both changes the rhythm of the year.',
			'en_meta_description' => 'Why early January feels wrong: the Gregorian calendar says advance while the body says not yet, and Aries is the real solar new year.',
			'en_content'          => '</p>
<p><u><em><strong>Text written by: Aria Milioni</strong></em></u></p>
<p><u><em><strong>Systemic Therapist</strong></em></u></p>
</p>
</p>
<p>Once upon a time — not in the sky, but on paper — human beings decided where the year should begin.</p>
<p>The Gregorian calendar was created to organise society, not consciousness; dated 1582, it was introduced by Pope Gregory. It aligns contracts, taxes, harvests, work, debts and systems of governance. Time became something that could be counted,</p>
<p>regulated, audited and controlled. The reason was this: for civilisation to work on a large scale, a common agreement was needed — and so 1 January was chosen as the starting line: clean, numerical, administrative.</p>
<p>This calendar governs the material agreement of life: bills to pay, deadlines, fiscal years, the school calendar, productivity targets. It belongs to the constructed dimension of reality, where continuity, control and predictability are essential. It does not answer to nature — it organises people.</p>
<p>And that is not a flaw. It is its function. And nothing beyond that.</p>
<p>But alongside this created rhythm, there is another year — one that does not begin by decision, but by alignment.</p>
<p>The solar return, in energetic and astrological terms, happens when the Sun enters Aries. That moment marks the true beginning of the solar cycle. It is when light begins to overcome darkness, when the Earth tilts once more towards growth, when life receives the signal to move forward. This is not symbolic; it is seasonal, biological, energetic.</p>
<p>Aries inaugurates movement. The seeds awaken. The blood warms. The systems spring into action. Long before calendars existed, life on Earth was already responding to this change. That is why many ancient cultures recognised spring — and not the middle of winter — as the true New Year.</p>
<p>The solar return governs energy, not administration.</p>
<p>It rules vitality, instinct, initiative, courage and birth.</p>
<p>It belongs to nature, to astrology, to time lived in the body.</p>
<p>So we live inside two simultaneous cycles, two dimensions of existence, two</p>
<p>timelines.</p>
<p>One begins in January and asks:</p>
<p>How will you manage your life?</p>
<p>How will you pay, plan, organise, maintain?</p>
<p>The other begins when the Sun enters Aries and asks:</p>
<p>How will you live it?</p>
<p>What wants to be born, to be initiated, to be embodied?</p>
</p>
<p>Winter — January, February and much of March in the northern hemisphere — exists between these two thresholds. By the Gregorian calendar, it looks like a beginning. By the solar calendar, it is still a closing.</p>
<p>That is why so many people feel discomfort in early January.</p>
<p>The system says “move forward”.</p>
<p>The body answers “not yet”.</p>
<p>Winter is the last chapter of the energetic year. It is the phase of fertile decomposition. The nervous system slows down. The psyche reviews. The body conserves. Expecting full performance during this period is not discipline — it is misalignment.</p>
<p>Caring for yourself while respecting both systems is learning to speak two languages.</p>
<p>● Mind: Use January to organise, not to launch. Plan without demanding immediate execution. Structure without pressure.</p>
<p>● Body: Honour low energy as functional, not as failure. Sleep more. Eat more densely. Move gently.</p>
<p>● Emotions: Allow introspection. Winter brings truths to the surface so that they do not sabotage spring. Emotions are information, not obstacles.</p>
</p>
<p>Then, when the Sun enters Aries, something changes naturally. Action stops being forced.</p>
<p>Decisions gain warmth. Direction becomes clear.</p>
<p>The Gregorian calendar keeps society running.</p>
<p>The solar return keeps you alive.</p>
<p>When both are honoured, life stops feeling like resistance — and becomes rhythm.</p>
',
			'link_map'            => array(),
		),
		'dois-fatores-que-fazem-o-seu-negocio-ter-consistencia-nas-vendas' => array(
			'en_slug'             => 'two-factors-that-give-your-business-sales-consistency',
			'en_title'            => 'TWO FACTORS THAT GIVE YOUR BUSINESS SALES CONSISTENCY.',
			'en_excerpt'          => 'Selling more is not the secret to a lasting business. How you welcome customers and the experience you create around them is what builds loyalty.',
			'en_meta_description' => 'How welcoming customers and a great buying experience build loyalty and consistent sales for your small business.',
			'en_content'          => '<p><em><strong>By Sonia Campos, Master\'s in Information Science and Specialist in Business Intelligence.</strong></em></p>
</p>
<p><strong>instagram: </strong><u><strong><a href="https://www.instagram.com/soninhafields/" rel="nofollow">https://www.instagram.com/soninhafields/</a></strong></u></p>
</p>
<p>In an increasingly competitive market, many entrepreneurs believe that the secret to success lies simply in selling more. However, the sustainability of a business depends on factors far deeper than a single commercial transaction. Among them, two stand out for their ability to generate loyalty, referrals and continuous growth: how you welcome the customer and the buying experience.</p>
</p>
<h5>The first contact is decisive. Even before assessing prices or terms, the customer assesses people. Friendliness, courtesy, lightness, good humour and genuine attention create an emotional connection that opens the door to trust. Showing mastery of the product or service conveys confidence, but knowing how to listen matters just as much. Many entrepreneurs make the mistake of presenting their solutions before understanding the customer\'s real needs. </h5>
</p>
<p>When we ask questions, listen attentively and seek to understand the challenges of the person in front of us, we can offer a more suitable, personalised solution. People like buying from those who convey positive energy, credibility and a genuine interest in helping them. </p>
<p>Excellent customer service may not generate an immediate sale, but it is a guaranteed future sale! </p>
</p>
<h5>The second factor is the buying experience. The relationship with the customer does not end when the sale is closed. On the contrary, that is the moment when loyalty starts to be built. Every detail matters: communication, customer service, delivery, follow-up and how the customer feels throughout the whole journey.</h5>
</p>
<p>Businesses that positively surprise their customers create a lasting memory. Delivering more than you promised does not necessarily mean spending more, but rather adding value through attention, care and excellence in the details. A small gesture can turn a satisfied customer into a true promoter of your brand.</p>
</p>
<p>In the end, consistent businesses are built by people who understand that selling is not just offering a product or a service, but creating relationships and memorable experiences. Customers may forget what they bought, but they rarely forget how they were treated.</p>
<p>That is what sets a simple sale apart from a sustainable business! </p>
</p>
<p>Sonia Campos</p>
<p>Entrepreneur and Master in Market Intelligence.</p>',
			'link_map'            => array(),
		),
		'entre-o-silencio-do-inverno-e-o-primeiro-sopro-da-primavera' => array(
			'en_slug'             => 'between-the-silence-of-winter-and-the-first-breath-of-spring',
			'en_title'            => 'Between the Silence of Winter and the First Breath of Spring',
			'en_excerpt'          => 'February is a quiet corridor between what has ended and what is still being born — a month of inner honesty rather than maximum productivity.',
			'en_meta_description' => 'February as a portal between winter and spring: why it can feel so intense, and how to move through it with rest, honesty and gentleness.',
			'en_content'          => '<p>(February as a portal of transition)</p>
<p><u><em><strong>Text written by: Aria Milioni</strong></em></u></p>
<p><u><em><strong>Systemic Therapist</strong></em></u></p>
</p>
<p>There is a moment in the year when life seems to breathe more slowly.</p>
<p>It is not the height of winter, when everything is already clearly withdrawn.</p>
<p>Nor is it spring yet, with its open promise of movement and expansion.</p>
<p>February is that sensitive interval — a silent corridor between what has ended and what</p>
<p>is still being born.</p>
</p>
<p>Energetically, it is a month that stirs deep layers.</p>
<p>Old emotions can reappear, tiredness becomes more visible, and a strange mixture</p>
<p>of impatience and apathy emerges. As if one part wanted to move forward&#8230; while</p>
<p>another still needs to rest.</p>
</p>
<p>Astrologically, February usually moves through <em><strong>Aquarius and Pisces</strong></em> — archetypes of</p>
<p>liberation and dissolution.</p>
</p>
<p>Aquarius opens windows. It questions patterns, breaks old mental structures and shows what</p>
<p>no longer fits the version of us that is emerging.</p>
<p>Pisces, soon after, softens our defences. It brings sensitivity and reveals where there is still pain</p>
<p>not yet felt, grief not yet processed, dreams forgotten.</p>
</p>
<p>That is why February can be emotionally intense even when, outwardly, nothing</p>
<p>“big” happens. Inside, a great deal is reorganising itself.</p>
<p>This is not a month of maximum productivity. It is a month of <em>inner honesty.</em></p>
</p>
<p>In the mind, it invites us to review narratives:</p>
<p>— Which thoughts no longer make sense for the person I am today?</p>
<p>— Which decisions do I keep postponing for fear of changing?</p>
<p>In the emotions, the invitation is to feel without haste — not to resolve everything, but to allow</p>
<p>old processes to complete themselves.</p>
</p>
<p>In the physical body, the request is simple and therapeutic: more rest than performance, more</p>
<p>warmth than demands, deep breathing, gentle stretching, slow walks.</p>
<p>The nervous system is still in winter mode.</p>
</p>
<p>And winter is not a mistake of nature — it is the laboratory where roots grow.</p>
<p>In the practical areas of life, February is a month of adjustment, not of expansion.</p>
<p>It is when we realise what truly deserves energy when spring arrives — what</p>
<p>continues, what ends, what needs a new form.</p>
</p>
<p>Spring does not arrive suddenly. It begins as a whisper: a day with more light,</p>
<p>a deeper breath, a new idea that appears effortlessly.</p>
<p>To navigate February wisely is not to force flowers before their time.</p>
</p>
<p>It is to allow:</p>
<p>● closing cycles without drama</p>
<p>● resting without guilt</p>
<p>● reviewing priorities honestly</p>
<p>● releasing habits that no longer sustain the next version of yourself</p>
<p>● caring for the body as fertile soil</p>
</p>
<p>If winter was the time to withdraw, February is the time to listen to what inside you</p>
<p>wants to be born.</p>
<p>And when spring finally opens — within and without — what was tended in silence</p>
<p>turns into natural movement, not effort.</p>
</p>
<p>Perhaps the true invitation of this month is not to do more, but to slow down enough to</p>
<p>notice who you are becoming.</p>
<p>Because it is in that space between the end and the beginning that life decides, with tenderness, what</p>
<p>your next form will be.</p>
</p>
<p>Aria Milioni</p>
<p><u><em><strong>Text written by: Aria Milioni</strong></em></u></p>
<p><u><em><strong>Systemic Therapist</strong></em></u></p></p>
',
