		'o-calor-que-nasce-do-inverno' => array(
			'en_slug'             => 'the-warmth-that-is-born-of-winter',
			'en_title'            => 'The Warmth That Is Born of Winter',
			'en_excerpt'          => 'Winter slows the world down — and asks us to choose what we want to see grow. A reflection on inner warmth, rest and creativity.',
			'en_meta_description' => 'Winter as a time to rest, choose what to nurture and light the inner warmth that keeps creativity and hope alive until spring.',
			'en_content'          => '<p><u><em>Text: Ana Luiza A Duarte</em></u></p>
<p><u><em>Integrative Therapist</em></u></p>
</p>
<p>Winter arrives with its dense air, its short days and a certain inevitable withdrawal. And, while the world seems to fall asleep, something in us begins to wake. It is the time to listen to what the body asks for, what the heart whispers, what the soul wants to preserve.</p>
<p>Cold is, at times, a form of care: it slows us down, preserves and protects what is still to bloom. And, since it is a time to conserve and prepare, perhaps winter is also an invitation to choose.</p>
<p>Before sowing the seeds, you need to know <strong>what you want to see grow</strong>. Which dreams deserve to germinate when the sun warms the earth again? Which ideas, affections or plans do you</p>
<p>want to nourish now, in the silence, so that they sprout strongly when the season changes?</p>
<p>Because inner warmth is not limited to the body — it can take the form of <strong>ideas that ignite</strong>, of <strong>intentions that warm up</strong>, of <strong>plans that take shape </strong>even under the cold.</p>
<p>They are small embers that keep alive the hope of a new flowering.</p>
<p>While outside everything seems still, inside us something reorganises itself. What looks like a pause is, in truth, preparation. Rest is the fertile ground of everything that is to come.</p>
<p>There is a kind of warmth that does not come from fire — it is born slowly, in silence, when the cold invites us to turn inward.</p>
<p>It is a warmth that springs from the heart and needs to be tended with care. The mind, when fed by prosperous thoughts, by ideas that inspire and by gestures that awaken creativity, helps to keep that flame alight. This warmth heals us, wakes us and allows us to give <strong>new ideas their first flight</strong> — small sparks that can bring us closer to ourselves and to the people around us.</p>
<p>Perhaps it is precisely this withdrawal that allows us to <strong>access our creative source.</strong></p>
<p>To create, we need to become sensitive to what surrounds us, to perceive the possibilities around us, to choose what inspires us and to transform it into something unique — an action, an expression, an idea that carries passion and determination. When the noise outside diminishes, we can hear those subtle voices within us, the ones asking for space, form and colour.</p>
<p>Winter, with its calm, creates the perfect ground to imagine and recreate what we want to live.</p>
<p>So light your small campfires: a book, a song, a hot soup, a good memory. Allow yourself that warmth that is born from within and spreads slowly.</p>
<p><em>Winter is a reminder that true warmth is not only in the sun — it is in what we choose to nurture when the world grows cold.</em></p>
</p>
<p><u><strong>Ana Luiza A Duarte</strong></u></p>
<p><u><strong>Integrative Therapist</strong></u></p></p>
',
			'link_map'            => array(),
		),
		'o-inverno-do-ego-um-renascimento-poetico' => array(
			'en_slug'             => 'the-winter-of-the-ego-a-poetic-rebirth',
			'en_title'            => 'The Winter of the Ego — A Poetic Rebirth',
			'en_excerpt'          => 'There is a winter inside every soul, where the Ego loosens its grip and everything that is excess begins to fall away.',
			'en_meta_description' => 'Winter as the sacred deconstruction of the Ego: how inner quiet, service and surrender prepare the ground for a poetic rebirth.',
			'en_content'          => '<p><u><strong>Text written by: Aria Milioni</strong></u></p>
<p><u><strong>Systemic Therapist</strong></u></p>
</p>
<p>There is a season within every soul in which everything grows quieter.</p>
<p>A gentle inner Winter, where the Ego loosens its control and everything that is excess begins to fall away.</p>
<p>Winter is not punishment — it is preparation.</p>
</p>
<p>It strips us bare with lightness, like trees letting go of their leaves, to reveal what is</p>
<p>true beneath the noise: procrastination, fear, resistance, the unconscious search for</p>
<p>validation.</p>
<p>All that limits our capacity to give, to evolve and to serve.</p>
<p>This is the sacred process of deconstructing the Ego — the clearing of the inner soil.</p>
<p>When we surrender, even in silence, we send our intention out to the Universe.</p>
<p>Not from the need of the Ego to receive, but from the readiness of the soul to grow.</p>
<p>True spirituality begins here: in honesty, in service, in the willingness to let old identities dissolve.</p>
<p>Winter teaches us our limits and our desires, what no longer belongs, and what still</p>
<p>pulses to stay.</p>
<p>And then, without effort, Spring arrives.</p>
<p>Spring is born when the Ego softens, when the inner ground thaws enough for new seeds to take root.</p>
<p>Suddenly, clarity turns into action, love turns into presence and the act of giving becomes the natural language of the heart.</p>
<p>There is no flowering without its Winter.</p>
<p>You do not plant in frozen soil.</p>
<p>You must allow yourself to be taken apart first.</p>
<p>This is the rhythm of healing:</p>
<p>Winter cleanses.</p>
<p>Spring is reborn.</p>
<p>And the soul, patient and luminous, crosses the bridge between the two.</p>
</p>
<p><u><strong>Text written by: Aria Milioni</strong></u></p>
<p><u><strong>Systemic Therapist</strong></u></p></p>
',
			'link_map'            => array(),
		),
		'o-que-todo-pequeno-empreendedor-precisa-aprender-para-fazer-o-negocio-crescer-por-que-entender-toda' => array(
			'en_slug'             => 'what-every-small-business-owner-needs-to-learn',
			'en_title'            => 'What Every Small Business Owner Needs to Learn to Grow Their Business. Why understanding every area of the company can be the difference between growing and closing your doors?',
			'en_excerpt'          => 'When you run a small business, doing everything yourself is normal. Here are nine areas worth mastering so your business can grow with confidence.',
			'en_meta_description' => 'A practical guide for small business owners: financial control, pricing, sales, marketing and more to grow with confidence.',
			'en_content'          => '<p>Hello, my name is Tatiane and this topic really struck a chord with me when I started Dunamase Hampers, and it matched Cristiane\'s Mini Interview (I\'ll leave the link here):</p>
<p><u><a href="https://tdcriativo.wixsite.com/brasileirosnairlanda/post/papo-de-empreendedor-com-um-toque-criativo-leve-e-motivador-para-inspirar-quem-pensa-em-empreende-13" rel="nofollow">https://tdcriativo.wixsite.com/brasileirosnairlanda/post/papo-de-empreendedor-com-um-toque-criativo-leve-e-motivador-para-inspirar-quem-pensa-em-empreende-13</a></u></p>
</p>
<p>To be very honest, I loved making gift baskets, but I discovered that I love everything that surrounds the world of entrepreneurship, and so TD Criativo was born, <u><a href="https://www.instagram.com/coachpatriciavidal/" rel="nofollow">https://www.instagram.com/coachpatriciavidal/</a></u> and then the ConexãoBr project <u><a href="https://www.instagram.com/conexaobr.ie/" rel="nofollow">https://www.instagram.com/conexaobr.ie/</a></u>, which is an arm of our Virtual Magazine (a recommendation especially from Patricia Vidal:) <u><a href="https://www.instagram.com/coachpatriciavidal/" rel="nofollow">https://www.instagram.com/coachpatriciavidal/</a></u></p>
</p>
<p><em>Starting a business</em> is, for many people, the fulfilment of a dream. The possibility of turning a skill, a passion or a market need into income leads thousands of people to start small businesses every year. However, there is a reality that is rarely shown on social media: at the beginning, the entrepreneur has to learn to perform several roles at the same time.</p>
</p>
<p>Before being able to hire specialised professionals or build a team, it is common for the entrepreneur to be the finance person, the salesperson, the one in charge of marketing and purchasing, the customer service contact and even the one who solves everyday problems.</p>
</p>
<p>Although it is challenging, understanding the basics of each area is not just a necessity — it is a strategy for the survival and growth of the business.</p>
</p>
<p>According to Michael Gerber (2001), many small businesses fail because the entrepreneur masters only the technical side of the service or product, but never learns to manage the company as a system. In other words, knowing how to do something well does not necessarily mean knowing how to run a business.</p>
</p>
<h5>1. Financial Control: Without Numbers, There Is No Management</h5>
</p>
<p>One of the greatest difficulties for small entrepreneurs lies in financial management.</p>
<p>Controlling income, outgoings, profits, expenses and cash flow is essential for the health of the company. Many businesses close not because they do not sell, but because they cannot properly manage the money that comes in.</p>
<p>According to Dornelas (2022), financial control allows the entrepreneur to make strategic decisions, reduce waste and have the predictability needed to grow.</p>
</p>
<p>Cash flow helps answer important questions:</p>
<p>&#8211; How much is my company really profiting?</p>
<p>&#8211; Am I charging enough?</p>
<p>&#8211; Can I invest right now?</p>
<p>&#8211; Am I mixing my personal money with the company\'s?</p>
</p>
<p>As Chiavenato (2021) states, “what is not controlled cannot be improved”.</p>
</p>
<p>Practical tip:</p>
<p>Even without hiring an accountant at the start, simple spreadsheets or finance apps can help with daily tracking.</p>
</p>
<h5>2. Pricing: Charging the Right Price Is Surviving</h5>
</p>
<p>One of the most common mistakes among small entrepreneurs is setting prices based on the competition or on guesswork.</p>
<p>Many charge only to “avoid losing the customer”, without calculating costs, time invested, materials, taxes, travel and profit margin.</p>
<p>According to Kotler and Keller (2019), pricing should take three main factors into account:</p>
<p>Costs</p>
<p>How much it costs to produce or deliver the service.</p>
<p>Perceived value</p>
<p>How much value the customer perceives in what you offer.</p>
<p>Positioning strategy</p>
<p>What image your brand wants to convey to the market.</p>
<p>When the price is badly calculated, the entrepreneur can work very hard and still make no profit.</p>
<p>As Sebrae (2023) highlights, financially sustainable companies need a clear pricing policy.</p>
</p>
<p>More information in this article with our dear Sonia</p>
<p><u><a href="https://tdcriativo.wixsite.com/brasileirosnairlanda/post/gest%C3%A3o-financeira-o-alicerce-invis%C3%ADvel-de-todo-neg%C3%B3cio-que-prospera" rel="nofollow">https://tdcriativo.wixsite.com/brasileirosnairlanda/post/gest%C3%A3o-financeira-o-alicerce-invis%C3%ADvel-de-todo-neg%C3%B3cio-que-prospera</a></u></p>
</p>
<h5>3. Sales Strategy: Those Who Never Learn to Sell Will Struggle</h5>
</p>
<p>Selling does not mean insisting or pressuring people.</p>
<p>In fact, selling means understanding needs and offering solutions.</p>
<p>Daniel Pink (2013) argues that, in today\'s world, we are all salespeople in some way — including entrepreneurs.</p>
<p>A good sales strategy involves:</p>
<p>Attract</p>
<p>Showing your product or service to the right people.</p>
<p>Talk</p>
<p>Understanding the customer\'s pain points and needs.</p>
<p>Close</p>
<p>Presenting solutions and making the buying decision easier.</p>
<p>Companies that invest in relationships with customers tend to sell more and build authority.</p>
</p>
<h5>4. Getting Paid: Professionalism Also Means Knowing How to Charge</h5>
</p>
<p>Many small entrepreneurs feel embarrassed or uncomfortable about asking clients to pay.</p>
<p>However, getting paid is part of running a business.</p>
<p>According to Robbins and Coulter (2020), organised processes reduce conflict and strengthen the professional image of the business.</p>
<p>Having contracts, defined deadlines, organised messages and clear communication prevents future friction.</p>
<p>Asking to be paid is not rude.</p>
<p>Asking to be paid is respecting your own work.</p>
</p>
<p>5. Purchasing and Stock Control</p>
<p>Buying too much can lead to waste. Buying too little can lead to lost sales.</p>
<p>Balance is essential.</p>
<p>According to Slack and Brandon-Jones (2022), good stock management reduces operating costs and improves the company\'s efficiency.</p>
<p>The entrepreneur needs to learn:</p>
</p>
<p>&#8211; How much to buy</p>
<p>&#8211; When to buy</p>
<p>&#8211; Which supplier offers the best value for money</p>
<p>&#8211; What actually sells</p>
</p>
<p>Being organised in this area prevents money from sitting idle and increases profitability.</p>
</p>
<p>6. Marketing and Social Media: Your Business Needs to Be Seen</p>
<p>Today, many companies have their main shop window on social media.</p>
<p>However, posting at random does not mean doing marketing.</p>
<p>Kotler, Kartajaya and Setiawan (2021) state that modern marketing involves relationships, positioning and building value.</p>
<p>Important questions:</p>
</p>
<p>&#8211; Does my brand convey trust?</p>
<p>&#8211; Does my profile look professional?</p>
<p>&#8211; Am I creating content that answers the customer\'s questions?</p>
</p>
<p>Companies that position themselves well on social media achieve greater reach, credibility and sales.</p>
</p>
<h5>7. Photos of Your Product or Service: First Impressions Matter</h5>
</p>
<p>On social media, the image sells.</p>
<p>A good photo conveys quality, organisation and professionalism.</p>
<p>According to Solomon (2020), consumers are highly influenced by visual cues during the buying decision process.</p>
<p>You do not need to start with expensive equipment.</p>
<p>But it is important to invest in:</p>
</p>
<p>&#8211; Good lighting</p>
<p>&#8211; A tidy setting</p>
<p>&#8211; Sharp images</p>
<p>&#8211; Before and after (when applicable)</p>
<p>&#8211; A professional visual presentation</p>
</p>
<p>Often, the customer buys with their eyes first.</p>
</p>
<h5>8. Customer Service and After-Sales: Good Customers Come Back</h5>
</p>
<p>Winning a customer costs more than keeping a satisfied one.</p>
<p>According to Kotler and Keller (2019), building customer loyalty increases profit and strengthens the brand\'s reputation.</p>
<p>After-sales can include:</p>
</p>
<p>&#8211; A thank-you message</p>
<p>&#8211; A request for feedback</p>
<p>&#8211; Promotions for long-standing customers</p>
<p>&#8211; Follow-up after the service</p>
</p>
<p>Well-served customers do not just come back — they recommend you.</p>
<p>And word of mouth is still one of the most powerful forms of marketing.</p>
</p>
<h5>9. Organisation and Strategy: Growing Without Direction Is Hard</h5>
</p>
<p>Companies do not grow through effort alone.</p>
<p>They grow through organisation.</p>
<p>Peter Drucker (2006) stated that efficiency is doing things right; strategy is doing what really matters.</p>
<p>Having goals, planning and vision helps the entrepreneur move out of survival mode.</p>
<p>Small consistent actions generate big results over time.</p>
</p>
<h5>Conclusion</h5>
</p>
<p>Being an entrepreneur requires courage, learning and adaptation.</p>
<p>At the start, it is normal to have to take on several roles. That does not mean failure — it means building.</p>
<p>The good news is that nobody has to know everything at once.</p>
<p>The secret is to keep learning, seek training and improve one step at a time.</p>
</p>
<p>As Peter Drucker used to say:</p>
<p>“The best way to predict the future is to create it.”</p>
<p>If you are a small entrepreneur, keep learning. Your business\'s growth begins with the knowledge you decide to acquire today.</p>
</p>
<h5>Bibliographic References</h5>
</p>
<p>CHIAVENATO, Idalberto. Introduction to General Administration Theory. 10th ed. São Paulo: Atlas, 2021.</p>
